{{!
    @template tool_vae/positioning_history

    The history of a rank: a sentence when there is no line; otherwise the heading of the line that stands and that line,
    then the heading of the earlier lines and each of them, the latest first.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\positioning_history. The template holds no logic.
    Every value is escaped (double braces) except one key:
    * linehtml - a line, drawn by the template tool_vae/positioning_line

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * none - object or null: text, the sentence said when there is no line
    * lines - array of {heading, linehtml}: heading is an object (text) before the first and the second line, null otherwise

    Example context (json):
    {
        "none": null,
        "lines": [
            {"heading": {"text": "Line that stands"}, "linehtml": "<div class=\"ms-3 mb-2\">Second statement.</div>"},
            {"heading": {"text": "Earlier lines"}, "linehtml": "<div class=\"ms-3 mb-2\">First statement.</div>"},
            {"heading": null, "linehtml": "<div class=\"ms-3 mb-2\">A first draft.</div>"}
        ]
    }
}}
{{#none}}<p class="text-muted">{{text}}</p>{{/none}}{{!
}}{{^none}}<div class="tool-vae-history">{{#lines}}{{#heading}}<h4 class="h5">{{text}}</h4>{{/heading}}{{!
}}{{{linehtml}}}{{/lines}}</div>{{/none}}
